# Adversarial Review — `fix/master-gate-and-dht-tests` (`746b2c34..1dce75af`)

## Method / admissibility (no shell available)
`tool_search` returned no `run_shell_command`, no `monitor`, and `web_fetch`/`skill` were declined. `git diff`/`git show` were therefore **NOT RUN**. The diff-of-record was reconstructed from: (a) the working tree, which is at the review tip — `.git/HEAD` → `refs/heads/fix/master-gate-and-dht-tests` = `1dce75af0feb…` (verified); (b) the branch reflog (`.git/logs/refs/heads/…`: `746b2c34` base → `e181a633` → ff → `9420936b` → ff → `1dce75af`); and (c) three engineer `*.findings.md` that embed verbatim hunks for `d787b76a`, `9420936b`, `1dce75af`. The `e181a633` (gate/closure) and `7c3534dd` (session/query/store/dht_test) hunks were not in a findings file, so those were reviewed against the **current tree state** (the "after" side), labeled accordingly. Line cites below are from the tip `1dce75af`.

## Findings

**P2 | `docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:406` (§3.1) vs `test/dao/host/gate_test.clj:977-999`** | The gate test `closure-totals-are-the-design-totals` asserts **151/149/147 files, 141 shared, 161 union** and its `testing` string attributes them to "§3.1 after the yin.repl DHT decoupling." But §3.1's latest amendment (r11 note, line 406) still states **146/144/145, 137 shared, 159 union**, and the `.md` is *not* in the diff. The committed `closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn` carry `:total 151/149/147` (verified by grep), so this branch regenerated the closure + test numbers but left the design authority contradicting them — the test's own name/citation ("the design totals", "§3.1") is now false, and an auditor cannot reconcile 151 against the doc. | Add an r-note to §3.1 recording the post-decoupling totals (151/149/147, 141 shared, 161 union) so doc ↔ committed closure ↔ gate test agree, or correct the test's §3.1 citation. (The *boundary itself is intact* — see verified-clean below; this is a doc/anchor drift, not a leak.)

**P3 | `src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:862-869`** | The `:recheck-after-input` hook fires only on a `nil?`→pending-run transition measured against the **post-`composition-recheck`** `state`. When a completing run's `fold-queued` (`repl.cljc:2657`) evaluates a *queued* `(require …)` that parks a **new** run, `state` already carries a pending-run, so the hook is skipped that tick; the shell `serve` that deposits `[:pending-run :links]` never runs, and `pending-text` renders the generic `;; require still pending` (no link name) until the next tick's `composition-recheck` names it. The direct-input path is correct and is covered by `live-loop-reports-the-name-of-a-new-pending-require`. | Also fire the hook when `rechecked`/`fold-queued` newly parked a run, or run one serve+recheck inside the fold-park path so the first notice is named. Low impact (one-tick delay, niche path: a require queued behind a completing require).

**P3 | `src/cljc/yin/shell/store.cljc:105-107`** | The composed-store refusal guards **both** `:content-store` and `:content-client`, but `a-dht-store-refuses-a-second-content-source` (`dht_test.cljc:1701`) exercises only `:content-store`. The `:content-client` arm is untested. | Add a case passing `:content-client` asserting it refuses (and, as the existing test does, that the directory is left unlocked afterward).

**P3 | `test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:91-104` & `:1012-1024`; `test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc:162-181`** | The serve→`recheck-pending` pump (`budget 32`, `(or resumed text)`) is duplicated verbatim across `eval-shell`, `type!`, and both files' `eval-at`. The head-test terminal branch keys on the literal string `";; require still pending"`, and the loop returns **silently on budget exhaustion** with no quiescence signal — a pathological case could assert against a non-settled state. Malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`): four copies will drift. | Extract one shared `drive-to-quiescence` helper; signal budget exhaustion (assert/throw) instead of returning silently; match the pending notice via a shared predicate/regex rather than an inline literal.

## Verified clean (no finding) — the substantive risk areas
- **`dao/space/dht.cljc:1496 busy?`** — removing `(seq (:order (:window node)))` is correct. Every **open** (`:waiting`) window entry is backed by `:fresh`/`:repair`/`:inflight`: `admit` (`:643-665`) only creates `:waiting` alongside a fresh queue entry or when already `attempting?`, and `release-entries`/`needed?` (`:577-609`) refuse to dequeue while `open-entry?` holds. `:failed` entries are **terminal** (`admit` short-circuits on `contains? … :entries`), so they initiate no work — exactly the failing idle case (two `::dht/solo` failed entries, empty queues). Unread ledger / loading / unreported-pub / fresh / repair / inflight checks all remain. Docstring's "settled" = "has an outcome" is consistent with `outstanding?`.
- **`yin/repl.cljc:2671-2674` parked-links retention** — necessary and correctly scoped. For a composed shell, `drive-links` uses `link/round-local`, which *cannot* serve a shell-owned link, so it returns empty `pending` while the VM stays `link-waiting?`; retaining `(:links parked)` (deposited by `session.cljc serve`'s `assoc-in [:pending-run :links]`, `:91-92`) is what lets `pending-text` name the link. Guarded by `(and (empty? pending) (link-waiting? vm'))`, so local-source drives (non-empty pending / halted) are untouched; `nil` links degrade safely to the generic notice.
- **`yin/shell/query.cljc:624` serve-publication target** — `repl/serve-publication` is engine→engine (`repl.cljc:1294`), so `(update after :engine …)` is the right target; for the shell composition (no `:publication :local-service`) it is a deliberate no-op and the second `serve` answers the parked call from its correlation. The prior bug (applying it to the wrong map) is fixed.
- **`yin/repl/main.cljc` hook ordering** — fires once per park: `composition-recheck` runs *before* `repl-step` and sees no pending-run that tick, so no double notice; `after-input` is appended last (`:881-884`) and flows correctly through `moved?` (`:887`, keeps cadence at base interval) and `prompt-owed?` (`:903`). The `(do (print prompt) (flush))`→`(print prompt)(flush)` change is cosmetic (inside `when`). Backward-compatible: compositions without `:recheck-after-input` skip the hook.
- **Gate A / host-boundary — genuinely enforced, NOT weakened.** The committed closure files contain **zero** references to `dao/jing/dht`, `yin/link/dht`, `yin/shell/dht`, `dao/space/dht`, `datagram`, or `yin/shell/{linker,query,session,completion}` (grep on the `.edn`, which demonstrably works — it found `yin/repl.cljc` and `:total`). Totals are cross-checked three ways (hardcoded `151/149/147/141` == `:total` field == `independent-traversal-agrees-with-the-committed-closure` (traversal B) == `161` union == `gate-files`). `list-2-equals-the-observed-calls` (`:1073`) asserts exact `(= list-2 observed)` — **no slack**, so effect ceilings cannot be silently raised. Injection negative-fixtures (`an-injected-host-arm…`, `an-injected-random-uuid…`, `effect-calls-escape-neither…`, `a-scan-failure-is-not-a-pass`) are present. `yin.repl.cljc`'s `{:random-uuid 4, :ambient 3}` and `main.cljc`'s `{:ambient 6, :clock 4, :print 14}` are unchanged by the diff (the hook adds no effect calls; the `print` de-`do` adds none).
- **`dht_process_test.clj:576` regex widening** — faithful, and actually *strengthens* the oracle. `published-line` is used only by `await-head-published` (`:587-594`), whose HEAD-equality check `(= last-published (head-of-dir dir))` is unchanged; widening to `(?:re)?published` makes a *bad* republication more likely to be caught (it becomes the `last` candidate and fails the HEAD comparison). There is an explicit republication scenario at `:1071` ("after A republished my.lib").
- **`dht_head_test.cljc` FIFO paren fix (`:1245-1275`)** — correct and additive: the `^:slow` FIFO `deftest` was previously **nested inside the prior deftest's body** (defined only at run time, so effectively never registered at load); it is now a proper top-level form. No assertion removed.
- **Cross-host (clj/cljs/cljd)** — no new reader conditionals; changed source is pure data / portable (`throw (ex-info …)`, the `print`/`flush` de-`do`). The `#?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error)` catches are pre-existing. The `.cljc` test files' lane constraints (requiring `yin.shell.dht`/`dao.jing.dht.mesh`) are pre-existing test-layer deps, outside the `yin.repl.main` closure-root, so they do not touch the Gate A invariant.

## Bottom line
No P0/P1. The five behavioral fixes (busy?, parked-links retention, recheck-after-input, serve-publication target, store refusal) are correct and well-integrated; the test edits faithfully track the composed-shell contract rather than relaxing it; the host-boundary invariant is genuinely enforced and not weakened. The one substantive issue is the **P2 design-doc/gate total drift** (§3.1 says 146/144/145 while the gate now asserts 151/149/147 and cites §3.1) — fix the doc or the citation. Three P3s (fold-queued notice latency, untested `:content-client` arm, harness duplication/silent budget exhaustion) are optional hardening.

